# This example demonstrates extended-Lagrangian charge equilibration
# (fix qeq/shielded/xlmd) with pair style reaxff.
#
# Auxiliary charge degrees of freedom propagated alongside the atoms replace
# the iteration to self-consistency: after a short warm-up with fully
# converged solves, each step applies only *xlcg* (default 1) conjugate
# gradient iterations.  The fix scalar (f_2 below) shows the number of
# iterations per step and thus warm-up and savings directly.  Compare with
# fix qeq/shielded (commented out below), which converges every step.

units           real
atom_style      charge

read_data       data.CHO
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (25 25 25)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  105 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.000 seconds

pair_style      reaxff NULL checkqeq no
pair_coeff      * * ffield.reax.cho H C O
Reading potential file ffield.reax.cho with DATE: 2011-02-18

neighbor        1 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes

variable        qtot equal charge(all)

velocity        all create 300.0 1281937
fix             1 all nve

fix             2 all qeq/shielded/xlmd 1 10.0 1.0e-6 400 reaxff
#fix             2 all qeq/shielded/xlmd 1 10.0 1.0e-6 400 reaxff xlcg 2
#fix             2 all qeq/shielded 1 10.0 1.0e-8 400 reaxff

thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 v_qtot
thermo          10
timestep        0.25

run             200

